      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "A",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">[...s]ix days in the month of Nisan, year 3 of the sabbatical cycle, which is year 4 thousand, six hundred and ninety-three</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[A.M] in Damascus, Samuel b. Abraham the Persian gave a ring of security for Khayriya, the virgin, daughter of Ezra\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... according to] the custom of the small synagogue, of the Babylonians. They fixed between themselves (a mohar of) fifty gold pieces: twenty-five,\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[the cus]tom of the con[gregation] and the remainder an addition for mohar. At the time of this security he advanced three fully weighed good gold pieces;</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[and] when he marries her he shall pay to her seventeen, the balance of twenty. May he be built by her. And th[i]rty will be delayed, \"on his neck.\"\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Man\u1e63\u016br b. Isaac, her guardian, [accepted for her this ring of security. She is a minor in his jurisdiction, and he shall pro[vide]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">for her [n]eeds until her marriage to her husband. And they are obligated to observe the stipulations of the congregation according to their laws and regulations. And he accepted, [Samuel]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[b. Abra]ham, all [this, as it is written and in] its time. And this writ of betrothal is valid. I, Mu\u02bfammar b.\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Ya\u02bfq\u016bb Benjamin ... I\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Aaron b. R. ...witness\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">\u2026 b. Saul ... Ya\u02bfq[\u016bb b.] Maym\u016bn, witness</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">...witness Abraham ha-shofe\u1e6d berrabi\u00a0 </li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
