      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "B",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">[...]six days in the month of Nisan, year 3 of the sabbatical cycle, which is 4 thousand and 693 years A.M.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... b.] Joseph ... [gave the ring of] security for Than\u0101, [the] virgin, daughter of Furayj ha-Kohen, according\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[to the custom of the small synagogue, of the] Babylonians [...]\u00a0 twenty-five gold pieces, the custom of the congregation\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] May he be built by her. And the remainder will be delayed, \"on his neck.''\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[ ... Ja]cob b. Nathan and Aaron b. Eli [may his Rock] guard him</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[ ... This writ of betrothal is valid in the l]aws (courts) of Israel.\u00a0 </li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
